 @UnluckyDomino  Obviously they want to save money as any company does but it's a fact that RDNA 1 and 2 have had no AI cores and since future features will likely focus a lot on these aspects there was no way that they would need to be handled differently when focus shifts more towards AI. I would completely agree that this part is AMD's fault and i would even call that incompetence from them but your assumptions about how they will handle this are just that.. assumptions. 

My problem is that people act like they know exactly what they are doing while none of it has been confirmed. I would agree with you if they really did what they said in their original statement but what you have said is simply not the case as of now so i won't trash a company for something they haven't done yet (other than missing out on driver features which was to be expected). It might be that they will only act when there is public outcry but that's exactly the problem that we don't know yet since we already knew that many features will not be compatible with RDNA 1 or 2 and therefore these generations could not be supported the same way the newer ones are.

Also their Driver support for Linux is by far better so i'm personally not really impacted by these Windows problems but i will obviously be against everything they have said in their original statement and have trashed them for that. I've only changed my mind because they seemed to have listened to the criticism and feedback so my original stance doesn't work anymore until i see their actions. If they act like you assume (which i know is not unlikely) i agree with you but i'm not one to act on assumptions.

